  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/zaireichthys_conspicuus.htm",
      "html": "<ul><li>Common name: Blotched sand catlet</li><li>IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/zaireichthys_conspicuus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Southern Africa: Upper Zambezi River from the rapid sections at Katima Mulilo down to just above the Victoria Falls.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/zaireichthys_conspicuus.htm",
      "html": "<p>Found in the rapid sections of rivers; seems to inhabit rocky rapids rather than sandy bottoms.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/zaireichthys_conspicuus.htm",
      "html": "<p>It feeds on insects.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/amphiliidae/zaireichthys_conspicuus.htm",
      "html": "<p>This species differs from Zaireichthys kafuensis, Z. kavangoensis, Z. monomotapa and Z. pallidus in having a premaxillary tooth patch with the buccal margin expanded laterally, and from all other species in its more robust form and bold markings.</p><p>Dorsal spines (total): 2; dorsal soft rays (total): 6; anal spines: 0; anal soft rays: 9–11; vertebrae: 34–35.</p><p>Etymology: the specific name 'conspicuus' refers to the conspicuous bold markings of this species.</p>"
    },
    {
